# A deliberately broken model for the model diagnostics exercise.
#
# WARNING: until the viewer drops or rejects the bad face, opening this file
# indexes past the end of the vertex list. Expect undefined behaviour in C++
# and an exception in C#.
#
# Problems, in order:
#   - vertex 6 is never referenced by any face
#   - face 3 has zero area (vertex 5 lies on the edge from 1 to 2)
#   - face 4 refers to vertex 9, which does not exist
# Faces 1 and 2 are fine and form a unit square.

o Broken Sample
v 0 0 0
v 1 0 0
v 1 1 0
v 0 1 0
v 0.5 0 0
v 3 3 3

f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
f 1 5 2
f 1 3 9
